 "notes": "Fig. 1 (plots/ma_fa.pdf in e-print), m_a [eV] vs f_a^-1 [GeV^-1]. Cosmological bound from recurrent axion-star explosions (axinovae) converting DM to dark radiation, derived from the decaying-DM constraint f_dDM <= 2.62% at 2 sigma (Eq. 16). Figure shows three nested excluded regions (green: conservative, T_osc=1 keV; red: power-law growth, T_osc=1 keV; blue: optimized over T_osc ~ sqrt(m_a M_pl)). Reported curve is the lower boundary of the blue region, the strongest bound and outer boundary of the total claimed exclusion (excluded region is at 1/f_a above the curve, i.e. f_a below ~10^7.8-10^16.4 GeV depending on mass). Curve extracted from vector paths with axis calibration from tick labels; bound is independent of SM couplings and of local DM density (assumes axions are all of DM, post-inflationary scenario).",
